WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:05.630
[music]

2
00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:08.130
[Instructor] Up to this point,
with all of our Prototypes,

3
00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:10.166
when you clicked run,
you would just get thrown

4
00:00:10.166 --> 00:00:12.260
right into the gameplay.

5
00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:16.090
No hello, no how are you,
just right to business.

6
00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:20.512
Then during run time, we've never
tracked score, lives, or progress,

7
00:00:21.012 --> 00:00:24.778
so there was no real way for the Player
to tell how they were doing.

8
00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:30.070
And finally when the game was over,
the only way to restart

9
00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:32.946
the game was to stop
the Project and rerun it.

10
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.540
Well in this Unit,
things are going to be different,

11
00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:40.020
because we are going to create
a Prototype that opens

12
00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:43.200
with a beautiful title screen
where the Player can choose

13
00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:47.240
the difficulty, then during
the game, the Player's score

14
00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:50.400
will be tracked and displayed,
and at the end

15
00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:53.390
there will be a Game Over
screen where the Player will be

16
00:00:53.390 --> 00:00:56.300
able to restart without
rebooting the entire application.

17
00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:59.873
That right there is
a five star user experience.

18
00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:04.650
All of those elements
you just saw, the title screen,

19
00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:08.145
menu buttons, score display,
and game over screen,

20
00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:12.640
fall into the all-important
mission critical category

21
00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:15.821
of User Interface, or UI for short.

22
00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:22.250
The UI includes any Text,
Buttons, or Display that the User

23
00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:25.051
can read or interact
with during their experience,

24
00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:28.035
and that is going to be
the focus of this unit.

25
00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:31.990
As you saw, having a UI
in your Project makes it look

26
00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:34.037
a lot more Professional,

27
00:01:34.037 --> 00:01:36.686
but it also allows your Project
to be fully playable.

28
00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:41.030
A fully playable game is one
that the user can experience

29
00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:44.530
seamlessly from end to end
without any game-breaking bugs

30
00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:48.640
or missing features.
Having a UI will finally allow for that.

31
00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:52.070
It is the missing piece
that will tie together everything

32
00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:54.090
you've learned up to this point.

33
00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:56.793
So without further ado,
let's start creating.

34
00:01:58.693 --> 00:02:00.861
[music]
